# Claude Code worktrees: isolated checkouts, never part of the tree
.claude/worktrees/

# Credentials. Carried into worktrees by .worktreeinclude, never committed.
.env
.env.local

# Personal, per-machine permission approvals. Project rules live in
# .claude/settings.json and ARE committed.
.claude/settings.local.json

# miniflare's own cache directory. It is created wherever a suite that drives
# the REAL plane is run from — bio-plane/ has always had one, and UI-13's
# intent-write harness makes one under civicos-ui/ too. Never part of the tree.
.wrangler/

# NEGATIVE-CONTROL PENS. A control driver copies pristine sources into a pen
# inside its own worktree (WORKER.md: never a shared scratchpad) and restores
# from them;
# RULED 2026-09-24 (BOB #33, 17:12Z, M0-172; THE PEN RULE block below states it in full): a driver's
# pen is the TOOL's own mechanism, not session scratch, so an in-worktree pen that is GITIGNORED and
# ITEM-NAMED stands; BOB #32's out-of-tree rule governs files a SESSION makes by hand. A per-run
# `mkdtempSync` pen outside the tree is the OTHER accepted shape — `bio-plane/test/frontier-chunk.control.mjs`
# pens that way since D-445 and so has no line here. (Restated at c20-batch27 by CONDUCT #20: D-445's
# first wording called the in-tree pen superseded, which BOB #33's ruling does not say.)
# UI-50's `.ui50-harness/` and UI-42's `.ui42-harness/` are the
# pattern. The drivers remove their pen on a clean run, but a driver INTERRUPTED
# mid-arm leaves one behind — and an untracked scratch file left in a worktree
# has already been swept into another item's walk (CLAIMS.md, UI-38's delegation
# to M0 about `bio-plane/test/op-claims.test.mjs`). Ignored so an interrupted
# control cannot become somebody else's corpus.
.ui*-harness/

# ---- THE PEN RULE (M0-182, 2026-09-24) — READ THIS BEFORE ADDING A PEN LINE BELOW ----
# A control driver's PRISTINE COPY NOW LIVES OUTSIDE THE WORKTREE. `bio-plane/test/pen.mjs`'s
# `controlPen(item)` is the one spelling — `mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), "nc-<item>-"))` — and
# `bio-plane/scripts/pensweep.mjs` grades every `nc-*.mjs` and `*.control.mjs` driver TEMP, MEMORY or
# IN-WORKTREE, with `test/pen-sweep.test.mjs` flooring the class at ZERO in-worktree pens. Why the move:
# since D-293 a gate on a dirty tree RECORDS NOTHING, so a control running beside a gate costs the gate;
# repository-walking suites WALK the pen (REC-185's `.rec185/` moved the battery's assertion total 19513 ->
# 19512 with no source change); and `gates.mjs` §2e reads the extra files as under-inclusion. BOB #32 ruled
# it (2026-09-24, `kickoffs/WORKER.md`), superseding "inside your own worktree".
#
# THE LINES BELOW STAND, and they are not leftovers. BOB #33 ruled (2026-09-24 17:12Z, M0-172) that an
# in-worktree pen which is DECLARED — gitignored and named for its item — is a driver's own mechanism; what
# BOB's ruling does not cover is an UNDECLARED one, a pen no line here names or one written beside its
# source as `${file}.pristine-<arm>`. M0-182 moved the `nc-*.mjs` class and the seven pens NO LINE HERE
# COVERED (`.m0110-harness`, `.m0109-harness`, `.m037-harness`, `.m0100-harness`, `.m0107-harness`,
# `.vf1-control-pristine`, `.m0111-harness`) and DELETED the 37 lines that then described nothing. Their
# per-pen reasons are in this file's history, at the commit that removed them.
#
# THE STANDING RULE ON SPELLING, kept here because M0-182 deleted the line that used to hold it
# (`.rec84-control-pristine/`) and thirteen notes below cited it: A PEN GETS ITS OWN LINE, NAMED FOR ITS
# ITEM, NEVER A GLOB. A wildcard over `.*-control-pristine/` or `.nc-*` would silently cover a pen nobody
# declared, which is the whole difference between a register that is re-affirmed and one that accumulates.
# ---- END THE PEN RULE ----
# PL-13's pen, same rule and named for its item rather than squeezed into the
# `.ui*` pattern: a plane-side control driver needs a pen too, and naming it
# `.ui…` so an existing line would cover it is the kind of small dishonesty that
# makes the next reader mistrust the whole file.
.pl13-harness/
# D-251's pen, same rule and named for its item for the same reason: an
# interrupted control run must not leave a copy of `pdfstructure.mjs` sitting
# untracked where the next walk can enrol it as a source file.
.d251-control-pristine/
# M0-134's pen (`bio-plane/test/finallyexit.control.mjs`), for the same reason: it arms six real suites.
.m0134-control-pristine/
# D-271's pen. Named for the item rather than the area because the item is a
# plane item; the `.ui*` spelling above is an accident of which area needed a
# pen first, not a rule about who may have one.
.d271-harness/
# D-266's pen, and its BASELINE CAPTURES too. Same rule, same reason for its own
# line rather than a widened `.pl*` glob. This item's driver arms `store.mjs` and
# restores from here, and the same directory holds the three instrument outputs
# the item quotes as its baseline — kept inside the worktree so no other session's
# battery can overwrite the figures this one reports.
.d266-harness/
# D-267's pen, named for its item for the same reason PL-13's is.
.d267-harness/
# D-280's pen, named for its item for the same reason D-267's and PL-13's are.
# An interrupted driver must not leave an untracked file that becomes somebody
# else's corpus (M0-15: `git stash -u` is repository-wide, not per-worktree).
.d280-harness/

# CASE-2's pen, named for its item for the same reason every one above it is.
# An interrupted driver must not leave an untracked file that becomes somebody
# else's corpus (M0-15: `git stash -u` is repository-wide, not per-worktree).
.case2-harness/

# D-310's pen, named for its item for the same reason every one above it is.
# An interrupted driver must not leave an untracked file that becomes somebody
# else's corpus (M0-15: `git stash -u` is repository-wide, not per-worktree).
.d310-harness/
.d311-harness/
# D-310's own run logs, kept INSIDE the worktree rather than in a shared temp
# root: the battery's residue check measured this session writing a baseline to
# /private/tmp and NAMED it as an unfenced shared path (D-237).
.d310-runs/

# macOS Finder artifact — committed once by CONDUCT on 2026-08-10 via `git add -A`.
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# FL-9's pen, named for its item for the same reason every one above it is. This
# driver arms sources in THREE trees (`agent-worker/src/`, `pdf-worker/src/` and
# `bio-plane/src/`) and renames `pdf-worker/node_modules` away for one arm, so an
# interrupted run leaving an untracked file where the next walk can enrol it as a
# source is exactly the hazard this line closes (M0-15: `git stash -u` is
# repository-wide, not per-worktree).
.nc-fleetbundles/

# CPDF-10's TWO pens, named for their item for the same reason every one above
# them is. This item's drivers arm sources in TWO trees (`ocr-worker/src/` and,
# for the queue row's chain-collapse arm, `bio-plane/src/`) and each REBUILDS the
# member's committed artifact between arms, so an interrupted run leaves both a
# pristine copy and a half-built artifact behind. An untracked scratch file left
# in a worktree has already been swept into another item's walk, and `git stash
# -u` is repository-wide rather than per-worktree (M0-15).
.cpdf10-pen/
.cpdf10-e2e-pen/

# M0-25's ARM-LIVENESS CENSUS: its per-driver logs and its own harness pen. The
# census RUNS every control driver in the estate and captures each one's whole
# output to a file (never a pipe — D-282), so a full run leaves ~88 logs behind;
# `.m025-anchor-harness/` is the pen the battery-side witness's own control driver
# copies pristine sources into. **This entry is not tidiness and it was earned in
# the same run it describes:** `check-firing.test.mjs` went RED on this item's own
# final battery because the census had run `refusal-codes.control.mjs`, which left
# `civicos-ui/test/.rec79-control-pristine/` behind, and check-firing's producer
# sweep read those pristine copies as a SECOND producer of a retired check. A
# driver's residue is not inert — it enters another suite's corpus — and a census
# that runs every driver makes that a certainty rather than a risk.
_m025/
.m025-anchor-harness/
# D-355's pens, each on its OWN line for the reason THE PEN RULE at the head of this section gives.
# REC-79's driver (`civicos-ui/test/refusal-partition.control.mjs`) wrote `.rec79-control-pristine/` on
# EVERY run from 2026-08-09 and never removed it, clean exit or red, and the pen was never listed here —
# it is the pen in the `check-firing` incident this block's note records. Since D-355 the driver removes
# each copy by name as its restore verifies and an exit hook removes the rest on every exit; SIGKILL
# cannot be caught, which is what this line is for. `.nc-d355-pen/` is `bio-plane/test/nc-d355.mjs`'s own.
.rec79-control-pristine/

# CAP-7's pen, named for its item for the same reason every one above it is. The
# Drive-link count streams ~1.4 GB of Oakland assets through this directory and
# deletes each file after reading it; an interrupted run leaves bytes behind, and
# an untracked scratch file in a worktree has already been swept into another
# item's walk (M0-15: `git stash -u` is repository-wide, not per-worktree).
.cap7-pen/
# M0-30's pen, named for its item for the same reason every one above it is. Its driver
# (`bio-plane/test/rowdesign.control.mjs`) arms `QUEUE.md`, `tools/plancheck.mjs` and
# `docs/architecture/CORPUS-STANDARD.md` and restores from pristine copies kept here. The
# driver removes the pen on a clean run and KEEPS it on a red one, where the copies are
# evidence; an interrupted run must not leave an untracked copy of a planning file where
# the next walk can enrol it as a second authority.
.m030-harness/

# CAP-12's control pen and its BASELINE checkout, each on its own line rather
# than under a glob — THE PEN RULE at the head of this section rules that a glob
# over `.*-control-pristine/` would silently cover a pen nobody declared, and the
# same argument covers a baseline worktree. The driver keeps per-arm pristine
# copies of `src/index.mjs` and `src/store.mjs` in the pen while it arms them; the
# baseline checkout is a pristine `origin/main` worktree this item measures its
# own baseline in, kept INSIDE this worktree because the shared scratchpad is not
# isolated between sessions (WORKER.md) and `git stash` is repository-wide.
.cap12-baseline/

# M0-31's pen, named for its item for the same reason every one above it is. The
# SEARCH §5 measurement streams the Oakland corpus through this directory — each
# body written, extracted and DELETED, so peak disk is one file — and keeps its
# per-document text log and its miniflare scratch databases here. An interrupted
# run must not leave an untracked copy of a corpus body, or a half-written log,
# where the next walk can enrol it (M0-15: `git stash -u` is repository-wide,
# not per-worktree).
.m031-pen/
# COFF-11's own working files: the LibreOffice grid probe that turned a vendor's figure into
# a measurement, its scratch workbooks, the logs its baseline and control runs were read
# from, and the scratch `git worktree` the pristine baseline was measured in. None of them
# is an input to anything; all of them are evidence that lives in the report and the release
# line instead.
.coff11-measure/
.coff11-baseline.log
.coff11-nc.log
.coff11-nc-cap12.log
.coff11-final.log
.coff11-ui.log
.coff11-coverage.log
.coff11-plancheck.log
.scratch-base/
bio-plane/.coff11-arm-wire-pristine.mjs
bio-plane/.coff11-arm-test-pristine.mjs
# FW-18's pen, named for its item on the standing rule every line above it
# follows. BREADTH §7 row 2 requires each content type to be written from a page
# that was actually FETCHED AND READ, so this directory holds the real Oakland
# documents of each class while they are read, the Tier-1 text extracted from
# them, and the control harness's pristine copies. A document body left untracked
# is a second corpus for the next walk to enrol — `coverage.mjs`'s fleet walk and
# the battery's discovery both read directories rather than a list — and an
# interrupted control run would leave one behind.
.fw18-pen/

# REC-94's pen (`bio-plane/test/nc-rec94.mjs`) and its pristine baseline worktree,
